---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PlaygroundShell from '../components/PlaygroundShell.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Classical Mechanics Atlas · Ganlin Xiang" description="Twenty-six interactive classical-mechanics experiments plus the original Physics Playground, built with native Canvas and tested numerical models." active="playground" canonicalPath="/playground.html">
  <main id="content" class="main playground-page"><div class="container">
    <header class="playground-hero reveal"><div><span class="eyebrow">Interactive Physics Atlas / Foundations + Mechanics I–II</span><h1 class="page-title-text">Physics<br /><em>Atlas.</em></h1></div><div class="playground-intro"><p>Turn undergraduate classical mechanics into linked motion, graphs, forces, energy maps, collisions, rigid bodies, oscillations, waves, and orbits.</p><p class="formula-note">Analytic solutions where possible; fixed-step RK4, Verlet, and mode decomposition where necessary. Every active instrument shares a bounded animation lifecycle.</p></div></header>
    <PlaygroundShell />
    <section class="playground-notes reveal" aria-labelledby="lab-notes-title"><span class="section-kicker">Lab notes</span><h2 id="lab-notes-title">What the instruments calculate</h2><div class="lab-note-grid"><article><span>ATLAS I / PARTICLES</span><h3>Motion, force &amp; energy</h3><p><code>ΣF=ma</code><br /><code>W=ΔK</code><br /><code>P=MV<sub>cm</sub></code></p></article><article><span>ATLAS II / RIGID BODIES</span><h3>Rotation &amp; vibration</h3><p><code>τ=dL/dt</code><br /><code>Mq¨+Kq=0</code></p></article><article><span>ATLAS II / WAVES &amp; ORBITS</span><h3>Fields of motion</h3><p><code>u<sub>tt</sub>=c²u<sub>xx</sub></code><br /><code>U<sub>eff</sub>=U+L²/2r²</code></p></article></div></section>
  </div></main>
  <script src="../scripts/playground/main.ts"></script>
</BaseLayout>
